From: telegram-custom <telegram-custom@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 00:03:30 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Eight accounts without Premium

Stock Telegram Desktop allows 3 accounts, plus one per Premium account,
up to 6. Main::Domain::kMaxAccounts 3 -> 8 and kPremiumMaxAccounts
6 -> 8, so Domain::maxAccounts() = min(premiumCount + 8, 8) is always 8.

Every use follows from the two constants: the add-account gate
(main_domain.cpp, settings_main.cpp, settings_information.cpp), the
over-limit check on account switch (core/application.cpp), and the
tdata bounds in storage_domain.cpp (accounts count and data#N index,
now < 8, so a tdata with up to 8 accounts loads). Per-account data
stays in data#N folders by index; existing accounts keep theirs.

A tdata holding more than 6 accounts will not load in stock Telegram
Desktop ("bad accounts count"); ours uses its own data dir, so the
pacman build never reads it. The Premium comparison list now shows the
accounts row as 8 / 8.
---
 Telegram/SourceFiles/main/main_domain.h | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Telegram/SourceFiles/main/main_domain.h b/Telegram/SourceFiles/main/main_domain.h
index 99e2c9d5b..9090b97f3 100644
--- a/Telegram/SourceFiles/main/main_domain.h
+++ b/Telegram/SourceFiles/main/main_domain.h
@@ -31,8 +31,8 @@ public:
 		std::unique_ptr<Account> account;
 	};
 
-	static constexpr auto kMaxAccounts = 3;
-	static constexpr auto kPremiumMaxAccounts = 6;
+	static constexpr auto kMaxAccounts = 8;
+	static constexpr auto kPremiumMaxAccounts = 8;
 
 	explicit Domain(const QString &dataName);
 	~Domain();
